commit 3eaeacee0285dd61239cf66336cf45358ec52f1d
Author: Anubhav Uttam <21anubhavuttam@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 14:21:40 2026 +0530

    fix(check): keep the suggested speed inside the voice's range
    
    Review on #63: a suggestion below the voice's slowest speed (Gnani
    0.85, ElevenLabs 0.7, Sarvam per model) would make the next render
    fail with a VoiceError.
    
    - VoiceEngine.speed_range(voice) reports the speeds a voice accepts
      (None: any); Gnani, ElevenLabs and Sarvam implement it, and their
      synth checks use it, so each range is stated once.
    - checks/audio.py holds the pace policy: PACE_TARGET = 165 next to
      PACE_MAX, suggested_speed(), and pace_warning(), which clamps the
      suggestion to the range and says when even the slowest speed won't
      reach the target, or when speed is already at its slowest.
    - tools.check looks up the voice a plain render uses (series.json,
      then MANIMVOX_VOICE, then the default) for its range.
    - Skills now say to use the speed check audio suggests instead of
      "0.9 first"; manifest regenerated; CHANGELOG entry updated.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

